  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Multi Country Border Security (MCBS) Programme in Jamaica, Haiti and the Dominican Republic</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed action aims to increase regional security in Jamaica, Haiti and the Dominican Republic. This will be done through (i) establishing a system for managing and exchanging information between law enforcement agencies; (ii) improving the capacities to monitor maritime and land borders against transnational organized crime, (iii) strengthening the investigation skills of LEAs, and their ability to mount joint operations in the interception and identification of organised crime organizations, (iv) increasing prevention and fight against the trafficking of persons.The first three components of this action will be implemented in partnership with an EU Member State agency (FIAPP) to guarantee adequate security expertise. The anti-trafficking component will be implemented by the International Organisation for Migration (IOM) given its specific mandate and technical expertise in the region.</narrative>
  </description>
